ochemical stains for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE and cytokeratin 14 were examined  on each of 3 blocks  The findings of these studies support the diagnoses being  rendered     The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor and  progesterone receptor will be reported in an addendum     GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     left breast biopsy   needle localization short superior  long lateral   single stitch anterior   is  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm  fragment of fibroadipose tissue with two localization  wires   a short stitch designating superior  a long stitch designating lateral   and a single stitch designating anterior  The long axis of the specimen runs  from medial to lateral  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue   posterior black  superior green and inferior yellow  The breast parenchyma  shows an irregularly outlined  tan pink to gray white  firm  nodule with dense  fibrosis adjacent to it  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  located 0 4cm from the nearest  superior margin and 0 8cm from the nearest anterior margin  The other margins  of excision are more than 1 0cm from the nodular lesion  The center of the  nodular lesion contains a metallic clip  The breast parenchyma lateral to the  nodular lesion shows another firm fibrous area  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  located REMOVED_DATE  cm from the nearest superior margin  The second metallic clip is not  identified  Submitted entirely and sequentially from medial to lateral in  cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing medial end margin  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representing lateral end margin  cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  through  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  representing the  entire nodular lesion with metallic clip in the center  and cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representing the entire fibrous appearing area lateral to the nodular lesion     Final 