Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 MAY 97 ACCESSIONED ON  20 MAY 97 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST PRIMARY INVADING DERMAL LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 97 at 15 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 MAY 97 at 15 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lesion  are four fragments of tissue  corresponding to breast tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  Each is sectioned to reveal no gross abnormalities  The fifth fragment of tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm skin ellipse excised to a depth of 0 9cm  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned with the ends submitted in A  and body in B  Additional fragment of breast tissue are submitted entirely in cassettes C   F  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   INCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
