Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 35 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 32     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO   Unknown  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  THE CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Katharine S  Kosinski  M D  THE CAMBRIDGE HOSPITAL  PATHOLOGY   REMOVED_CASE_ID  CAMBRIDGE STREET CAMBRIDGE  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  Susan Pories  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  08 JUN  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  1 Blocks  1   report_end  , Not_reported.
