Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 13 CLINICAL DATA  History of carcinoma of the right breast  by FNA  Now undergoing right modified radical mastectomy  Cytology positive                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  SPANNING 6 CM AND EXTENSIVELY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 11 OF 14 LYMPH NODES AND TRANSGRESSING THE CAPSULES OF SEVERAL LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the mastectomy specimen appear free of the tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   A few tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 24     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING FOR HER 2 NEU  CERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   ONCOPROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for Her 2 neu  cerb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   oncoprotein  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 03     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of tan very firm tissue  half frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remainder submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axilla  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  consisting of a right breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  an overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm with a unremarkable nipple and a 3 5cm incisional wound with 