 REMOVED_CASE_ID  GATES LIORA L 49 F  REG REF 11 17    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC KAHAN MORTON G  M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  11 17 06  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Palpable areas of hypoechoic shadowing  history of multiple benign right breast biopsies  poorly defined  extremely dense breasts  carcinoma Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast biopsy  right breast at 12 o clock  and consists of six firm  tan white  glistening needle biopsies with attached blood clot ranging in size from 1cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 1 9cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter  Entirely submitted in cassettes REMOVED_DATE 6X all  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  12 o clock  needle biopsy  Infiltrating lobular carcinoma  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  The invasive tumor measures at least 1 0cm  in size  In this limited sample  the histologic grade is 2 of 3  No lymphatic vascular invasion identified  Immunostains for estrogen and progesterone are in progress  results will be reported in an addendum  Final Diagnosis by  Jean L  Fraser  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD Notes  REMOVED_DATE  Slides lost per Steve   B W Hosp  jam  CR  REMOVED_DATE Per Desayda at DFCI  sent 2 slides 1 2L and 2 2L to Path Proc   BOC  Smith 117A  REMOVED_DATE rjs dg CO Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT GILD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ ADDENDUM REPORTAddendum  1 Entered  11 21 06  REMOVED_CASE_ID      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION     This report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  The original diagnosis is unchanged  Immunohistochemical staining performed on formalin fixed  paraffin embedded block 2 reveals the following results for the infiltrating carcinoma  Estrogen receptor  POSITIVE Progesterone receptor  POSITIVE Estrogen receptor  antibody 6 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   avidin biotin complex detection  and progesterone receptor  antibody PgR 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   avidin biotin complex detection  quantitation of the percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  POSITIVE   10  of nuclei stained POSITIVE  focal  1 to 10  of nuclei stained POSITIVE  rare   1  of nuclei stained NEGATIVE  0  of nuclei stainedAddendum Final  FRASER JEAN L  MD      REMOVED_DATE  11 21 06  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD FRAJE Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Antibody  NOS BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Positive BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Obstruction  NO BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Tumor cells  un BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Carcinoma  NOS BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Lobular carcino BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX NCA BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Complex BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX For BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Progesterone BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Estrogen  NOS Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCOPIES TO  KAHAN MORTON G  M D   REMOVED_CASE_ID  WASHINGTON ST   SUITE 365 NEWTON  MA REMOVED_DATE PETERS HOPE M D  NWH DEPT OF RADIOLOGY NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID  HEPETERS PARTNERS ORGMARKERS  Breast Disease Related  Consult Case Out  Consult Case Return  Tumor case Edited by  REMOVED_DA