Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 55 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  Rare tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 30     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm piece of fiberadipose tissue with attached REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  medial blue  superioral green  lateral red  inferior yellow  deep black  A representative section of the closest resection margin  deep  is frozen as FX 1  now in A  A representative section of the mass is frozen as FX 2  which was saved for further studies on Cox 5  The hard  pink white mass is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in greatest dimension and is 0 7cm deep to the skin  The mass is surrounded by fibrous tissue  some of which extends to the deep margin of resection  The rest of the specimen is unremarkable  Section code  B E representative sections of breast mass F G fibrous tissue on either side of mass H  lateral and superior margins of specimen Labeled  left axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of grossly unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Eleven lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm in greatest dimension are submitted in I L  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  DEEP MARGIN  IN SITU CARCINOMA PRESENT APPROXIMATELY 1MM FROM DEEP MARGIN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  TUMOR  LEFT BREAST   INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SAVE TO COX 5  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE U