Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  55 Fruit Street  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  E   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  72   Sex  M  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   WHITE 8  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 09 59  Results To   Steven Lawrence McAfee MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  LIVER CORE BIOPSY  LEFT   Centrilobular hepatocyte atrophy  necrosis and hemorrhage consistent with  congestive hepatopathy  see note      Note  The biopsy demonstrates marked hepatocyte atrophy and ischemic necrosis in  a predominantly zone 3 distribution and effecting approximately30  of the  hepatic parenchyma  Hemorrhage  mild mononuclear inflammation  and histocytes  are also identified in theses areas  Sinusoidal dilation is present  Central  veins are patent  Portal areas show focal ductular proliferation with no  significant inflammation  Trichrome stain shows moderate sinusoidal fibrosis   Reticulin stain highlights foci of attenuated hepatic cords in areas of  congestion and hemorrhage  An iron stain shows mild patchy  1  to 2   iron  deposition within hepatocytes and Kupffer cells  PAS D stain shows no  intracytoplasmic globules and highlights macrophages within areas of hepatocyte  necrosis  There is no evidence of malignancy     The differential diagnosis for these congestive changes includes the many causes  of hepatic venous outflow dysfunction  including Budd Chiari and cardiac  disease   Clinical correlation is advised            Electronically Signed Out By Jamie M Everett MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed o