hed  and in no  acute distress  The right breast showed a 0 7cm  approximately 2cm from the lateral  periareolar scar  non tender  well defined  round  firm and mobile nodule     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lesion  that was well defined  round  solid  homogeneously  hypoechoic without  significant internal or notable peripheral vascularity     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy was performed by palpation     2 aspirates were performed using 23 gauge needles without local anesthesia and  without complications   1 slide was stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by  Martha Pitman  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  The physician assistant was notified of the preliminary results by  personal communication at 1 40 p m           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation          Electronically Signed Out By  Martha Bishop Pitman MD on REMOVED_DATE 10 00       CLINICAL HISTORY  Breast invasive ductal carcinoma in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  lumpectomy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID           SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  RIGHT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  RIGHT  Received 1 slides in ETOH  Received 1 air dried  sli