situ  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptors  Requested NOTE  The lobular carcinoma cells stain for keratin 903 but do not stain for e cadherin  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 10                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block T   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 26 Proofread by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm piece of tan red adipose tissue with a guide wire running through it  A bow tie stitch marks the superior margin  a long stitch marking the lateral margin  and a short stitch mark the anterior margin  Between the anterior and lateral stitch markings there is a skin ellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and contains no lesions  The entire specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow and sectioned along the medial lateral axis from medial to lateral to reveal yellow unremarkable appearing adipose tissue as well as white fibrous appearing tissue  with no obvious identifiable lesions visually  Upon palpation the specimen appears to be diffusely nodular  There is one discrete nodule that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and appears tan white  Representative sections of the specimen are placed in cassettes A J with the suspicious lesion in cassette E  The skin ellipse was a serially sectioned and entirely placed in cassette AA  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm unoriented piece of adipose tissue  The specimen is to reveal a firm tan white homogenous mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes K P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final inferior margin long suture inferior margin  short bracket inferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 9cm piece of adipose tissue with a very long and four short stitches marking the extent of the true margin  The entire margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal yellow adipose tissue with numerous white firm fibrotic appearing bands throughout the tissue  and a discrete white fibrous appearing mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and lies 1 2cm from the inked margin  Representative sections all including the margin are placed in cassettes Q Z with samples containing the suspicious mass in cassettes Q W  The skin ellipse was serially sectioned en face and entirely submitted in cassette AA  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  LUMPECTOMY PART B  BREAST RIGHT ADDITINAL INFERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN  EXCISION , Not_reported.
