rminations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm firm  tan white ill defined area  The entire lesion is submitted in cassette A through E  Representative sections of firm area adjacent to lesion in cassette F and G  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision   additional margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast  entirely submitted in cassettes H through M  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in N through R  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SUSPICIOUS AREAS  NOT LARGE OR HOMOGENOUS ENOUGH FOR FROZEN RECEPTORS  NO FROZEN TAKEN  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASS   PART B  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN   , No.
