Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM AS MEASURED IN A GLASS SLIDE  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III   PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  WITH A SINGLE FOCUS SUSPICIOUS FOR LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MIXED INTERMEDIATE AND HIGH GRADE  WITH COMEDO NECROSIS AND CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definitive blood vascular invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab and accompanied with specimen radiograph   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm segment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a localizing wire  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm  tan white  firm  stellate mass which is 0 3cm from the inked margin  Representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  The remainder was entirely submitted in cassettes A through K with suspicious area in A through F  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES AND A SUSPICIOUS FOCUS OF INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Yes.
