Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 47 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  In situ carcinoma is not recognized  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a single piece of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  white  highly suspicious lesion  grossly approaching very close to the resection margin  The specimen is submitted in toto in cassettes A through G  lesion in A and B   Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  VERY SMALL LESION  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY    report_end  , No.
