Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue  Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  ESTHER RHEI M D   CASE  BS 06  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Resident  Wai Chin Foo  M D   Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D   PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST  CENTRAL POSTERIOR  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS   Apocrine cysts with calcifications   Epithelial hyperplasia   Skeletal muscle fragment   Note  No carcinoma is seen after complete microscopic examination of the  specimen  including margins   CLINICAL DATA   History  A 51 year old female with history of Hodgkin s lymphoma and thyroid  cancer  s p chemotherapy and radiation  Now with L central posterior  mammographic calcifications not amenable to core biopsy due to severe pectus  excavatum and deep location   Operation  Lt breast wire localized biopsy   Operative Findings  Not given   Clinical Diagnosis  Abnormal L mammogram   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Left breast tissue wire loss of consciousness short stitch superior long  stitch lateral whipstitch chest wall margin   RADIOLOGY   Wire and calcifications in specimen  OR called  Dr  Twohig   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   and  left breast tissue   and consists of a tan yellow lobulated portion of  fibroadipose breast tissue  3 5cm superior to inferior  1 0cm medial to  lateral  and 4 2cm anterior to posterior   There is a short suture  designating the superior margin  long suture designating the lateral margin   and whipstitch designating the chest wall margin  The specimen radiograph  reveals a wire and faint calcifications  There is a needle localization wire  in place entering through the anterior medial aspect of the specimen  The  specimen has been previously inked per pathology protocol  superior red   inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  anterior blue