Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Non Gyn Cytology Report        Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  A   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  48   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Institution  MGH  Location  WRN 219  PATH FINE NEEDLE  Date of Collection  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 14 51  Results to   Erin Keefe Sullivan NP        FINAL DIAGNOSIS    A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT     SPECIMEN ADEQUACY   Satisfactory for evaluation     INTERPRETATION   NO MALIGNANT CELLS IDENTIFIED     DIAGNOSIS   Benign appearing groups of cohesive ductal cells with accompanying myoepithelial  cells   Proteinaceous fluid and few macrophages  suggestive of cystic change     Note These findings may be seen in association with fibrocystic change       This case has been reviewed by Dr  Darcy Kerr  fellow in cytopathology         Electronically Signed Out By  Rebecca Ann Osgood MD    Diane Kuebler  CT ASCP     By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis           PROCEDURES ADDENDA  Rapid Interpretation    A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT   FNA Rapid Interpretation     Benign breast parenchyma and cyst contents     This case has been reviewed by Dr  Darcy Kerr  fellow in cytopathology            Electronically Signed Out By  Ivan A Chebib MD on REMOVED_DATE 09 49     Patient Evaluation and Management  with Interpretation     Chief Complaint  This 48 year old female was referred to the Pathology Fine  Needle Aspiration Biopsy Service by Erin Sullivan  NP for consultation and  diagnosis of a lesion in the left breast     Clinical History  Left breast lump  self palpated  x 1 month  History of right  breast ADH  Sister  49 y o  with breast carcinoma  Lump is benign on imaging and  consistent with fibrocystic changes on clinical exam     Physical Exam  The left breast showed a 1 2cm non tender  well defined  ovoid   rubbery and mobile mass at 4 o clock  2cm from the areola     Ultrasound was used to evaluate the lesion and showed a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  lesion that was  ill defined  ovoid  solid and cystic and heterogeneously  hypoechoic and isoechoic     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     Three aspirates were performed using 25 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   4 slides were stained for immediate evaluation  Additional tissue was submitted  for further evaluation     The procedure was performed by Darcy Kerr  Fellow     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  Erin Sullivan MD was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 5 00 p m           The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Ivan A Chebib MD on REMOVED_DATE 10 14       CLINICAL HISTORY  Left breast lump for 1 month         SPECIMEN SOURCE  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT  Received 3 slides in ETOH  Received 3 air dried  slides           Specimen  BREAST FNA BIOPSY  LEFT   