Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  13 AUG 97 at 09 50 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE SUPERIOR MARGIN  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  ADJACENT TO THE MASS  NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is seen  BREAST  RIGHT DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  NEW SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 5 LYMPH NODES WITH FOCAL EXTENSION BEYOND THE LYMPH NODE CAPSULE  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 AUG 97 at 17 10                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 AUG 97 at 08 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number in four portions  Labeled  right breast tissue  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 stellate gritty lesion with focal fibrous extension to the superior margin  Representative section of the superior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in A  Three additional representative sections of the lesion are submitted in B D  The tissue away from the lesion is submitted in E G  Labeled  right breast  new deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked entirely  representative sections are submitted in H J  The cut surface of the specimen is unremarkable  Labeled  new superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm breast tissue with staple at old margin  The new superior margin is inked  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no grossly obvious lesion at the new margin  Representative sections are submitted in K M  Labeled  axillary nodes  right  is an aggregate of fatty tissue with lymph nodes  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The lymph nodes are dissected  and representative sections are submitted in N R  Resident  IVANA DELALLE  MD  PHD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   SUPERIOR MARGIN  TUMOR EXTENDING CLOSE TO SUPERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                           