Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  16 MAY 95 at 19 02 CLINICAL DATA  Infiltrating tubular carcinoma of the right breast  0 8cm  with unknown margins                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   0 8 CM  95   PRESENT AT THE INFERO DEEP MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  FEW FOCI   5   IN A BACKGROUND OF EXTENSIVE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  BIOPSY SITE WITH CHRONIC INFLAMMATION  AND FAT NECROSIS  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  APOCRINE CYSTS  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  AND A FIBROADENOMA  5  SKIN  SCAR  NOTE  Most of the infiltrating carcinoma is in a tubular pattern  however  a few nests of more solid  infiltrating tumor are present  The small focus of infiltrating carcinoma present at an inked infero deep margin shows cautery artifact  Immuno  histochemical stains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be reported as an addendum  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 22 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 95 at 20 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two separate specimens  Labeled  right breast mass  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast re excision specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm overlying skin ellipse containing a 2 0cm central  well healed scar  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm area of fat necrosis  0 7cm below the skin ellipse  surrounded by a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm rubbery  solid  and partially cystic tan gray mass which abuts the superior and deep margin in the lateral half of the breast  The medial portion of the breast is unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  Labeled  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary node dissection containing multiple nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 1cm in greatest diameter  SECTION CODE  A B  Superior and deep margins  C D  Inferior and deep margins  E  Lateral margin  F  Medial margin  G  Skin in biopsy tract  H L  Lymph nodes  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Steven Joseph Nisco  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT MASS  PART B  BREAST  AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , No.
