n previously performed on the majority tumor  see addended report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE kg  40 5cm x 28 5cm x 5 4cm mastectomy specimen consisting of breast and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  There is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm piece of paper labeled  3M Comp  also received with the specimen  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior is inked black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 22 4cm tan skin ellipse is notable for a 12 7cm linear scar in the right outer quadrant that is 2 8cm from the REMOVED_DATE x 5 6cm tan brown nipple areolar complex  A 4 4cm linear scar in the far right upper outer quadrant is located 1 6cm from the axillary tail  Three well circumscribed red telangiectatic areas measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm are located on the skin  1 4cm  8 2cm and 4 2cm respectively from the areolar complex  The posterior margin of the mastectomy specimen is smooth  and has scant strands of muscle and several small ligatures  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm healing biopsy site in the breast  deep to the 12 7cm linear scar  associated with scattered ill defined firm areas  The closest posterior margin to the breast biopsy cavity is 5 5cm  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm area of ill defined region of induration and fat necrosis in the axillary tail  consistent with healing biopsy site  deep to the 4 4cm linear scar near the axillary tail  and this area is 0 5cm from the posterior margin  The rest of the specimen reveals multiple fibrous areas  Six lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary region  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 4cm  SECTION CODE   REMOV