ceptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 15 11     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan yellow  rubbery piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a white rubbery well circumscribed moveable mass  measuring 0 9cm in greatest diameter  No frozen section done  Representative sections are submitted in A through J  The sections of the well circumscribed mass are in E and F  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST   SMALL  0 9CM  FREELY MOVABLE NODULE AT PERIPHERY SOFT IN CONSISTENCY  NO OTHER LESION  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Not_reported.
