east  There is residual infiltrating lobular carcinoma  present around the hematoma site measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  No vascular or  lymphatic vessel invasion is seen  The previous needle biopsy is  reviewed  S 01  REMOVED_CASE_ID    The lobular invasive cancer extends to within  1 0mm  of the deep  posterior  margin   Specimen D contains two foci of infiltrating duct carcinoma  One is at  10 o clock  is residual and the size is estimated at 2 0cm  The 6  o clock site is residual and the size is estimated at REMOVED_DATE 5cm  Focal  lymphovascular invasion is seen  The 10 o clock focus is free of inked  anterior and posterior margin  greater than 1 0cm  from each   The 6  o clock focus extends to within 1 0mm  of the deep  posterior  margin   Diffuse extensive ductal carcinoma in situ is seen near both residual  invasive tumor foci and hematoma cavities  both estimated as involving  a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  area  The previous biopsies are reviewed  S 01  REMOVED_CASE_ID     Estrogen and progesterone receptors and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu will be done on blocks   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and reported in an addendum   Final Diagnosis by  Dennis J  Feen  M D   INTRA OPERATIVE CONSULTATION   OPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION  TISSUE EXAMINATION    Left and right sentinel lymph nodes  Blue nodes  no gross tumor present   RJS  Clinical diagnosis   history   Bilateral breast cancer  Tissue Designation   A Sentinel lymph node   left axillary  B Sentinel lymph node   right axillary  C Breast  simple mastectomy   left  D Breast  simple mastectomy   right  E Lymph node  biopsy   right axillary  F Skin  excision   right lower chest wall  G Skin  excision   left upper chest  H Skin  excision   left lower chest  Gross description   The specimen is received in eight containers   Specimen A is received in formalin  labeled  left sentinel lymph node  and  consists of a lymph node which measures 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  and has a bluish brown  tinge to it  There