Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 14 CLINICAL DATA  Previous needle localization  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   outside path reviewed here  reported as lobular carcinoma in situ with small invasive component and DCIS on right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  TWO FOCI  3MM AND 1MM  SEPARATE FROM BIOPSY CAVITIES  RESIDUAL LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY CAVITIES  Note  The resection margins are negative for carcinoma  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Receptor studies will be reported separately  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  NOTE  Keratin stains will be reported separately  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY SECONDARY SENTINEL  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Keratin stains will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 05                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Immunohistochemical stains for keratin performed on the two sentinel lymph nodes show no keratin positive tumor cells in the lymph nodes  Added by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 22     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Four specimens are received  Labeled  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 17 0cm skin ellipse containing an unremarkable areola nipple complex and a suture designating the superior aspect  The deep margin is inked in black while the anterior aspect is inked in blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity with a stellate shaped area of fibrosis radiating up to 2 0cm from the biopsy cavity and located 2 0cm from the nearest  deep  margin  The biopsy cavity itself is 0 8cm from the anterior  nearest  margin and 4 0cm from the deep margin  The surrounding breast parenchyma is fibrous with focal areas of cystic change  There is a second biopsy cavity located 8 0cm superior to the larger biopsy cavity  The smaller  superior cavity measures 1 0cm in greatest dimension with a stellate shaped area of fibrosis  abutting the anterior margin and 1 0cm from the deep margin  The biopsy cavity itself is 1 0cm from the deep  nearest  margin and 1 0cm from the anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma has scattered areas of rubbery  tan white  fibrous parenchyma with scattered cystic changes  SECTION CODE INFERIOR BIOPSY CAVITY A  Nearest anterior margin  B  Nearest deep margin  C  12 o clock   deep  D  1 o clock  E  5 o clock  F  6 o clock  G  8 o clock  SUPERIOR BIOPSY CAVITY H  Nearest deep margin  I  Nearest anterior margin  J  Scar at anterior margin  K L  Representative section of biopsy cavity  M P  Representative sections of breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavities  Labeled  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm lymph node  Bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette Q  Labeled  secondary right axillary sentinel node  are two lymph nodes measuring 1 0cm and 1 5cm in greatest dimension  the smaller is inked in black  Both are bivalved and submitted entirely in R  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  double suture   superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm mastectomy specimen with an overlying portion of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm containing a double suture designating the superior aspect and an unremarkable nipple areola complex  The deep margin is inked in black while the anterior lateral aspect is blue and the anterior medial aspect is green  Sectioning reveals a 2 0cm area containing firm  tan white nodules ranging in size from 0 4cm to 0 5cm in greatest dimension and located 3 5cm from the nearest  deep  margin  The remaining breast parenchyma reveals areas of dense  tan white  fibrous parenchyma with focal cystic changes  SECTION CODE S  Deep margin  T U  Firm nodular area  V  Nearest anterior medial margin  W BB  Representative sections of breast medial to lateral  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS F