ing assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm area of cysts and fibrosis with a central 0 5cm area of calcification  This area abuts the margin  This area is submitted entirely in cassettes A through D  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted in cassettes E through F  Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   CYSTS AND FIBROSIS  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , No.
