Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  L   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  60   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 18 13  Results To   Adam Scott Feldman MD  MPH      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  LEFT ADRENAL GLAND  ADRENALECTOMY   Adrenocortical carcinoma  8 0cm    see note      Note  The tumor has almost completely replaced the adrenal gland with only a  compressed  thin rim of unremarkable adrenal parenchyma identified  The  neoplasm is comprised of sheets of eosinophilic tumor cells with high nuclear  grade  increased mitotic activity   5 10 HPF   atypical mitosis  extensive  necrosis  comprising  50  of the tumor   lymphovascular invasion and capsular  invasion  The tumor focally bulges into the peri adrenal soft tissue surrounded  by a thin fibrous capsule  without definitive evidence of invasion   Immunohistochemical stains reveal the tumor cells are positive for  synaptophysin  Melan A and inhibin  and negative for pancytokeratin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Cam5 2   supporting the diagnosis  The capsule was focally disrupted  making it difficult to assess the margin  although there seems to be a thin  fibrous capsule in some areas at this site  All other resection margins are  uninvolved  with tumor measuring  1 0mm to the nearest inked soft tissue  margin  Dr  Vania Nose has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis   The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  AJCC  7th edition  Stage  p REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Nx  Mx        Electronically Signed Out By Kristine M Cornejo MD       Resident Pathologist   Jonathan S England MD      By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 AND  1A   LEFT ADRENAL GLAND    Primary adrenocortical neoplasm with necrosis  Defer to permanents for final  diagnosis  Case discussed with surgeon     Kristine M Cornejo MD    Other Pathologist s    Declan McGuone MBChB  Nicholas A Zane MD  PhD    CLINICAL HISTORY  Adrenal mass     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  LEFT ADRENAL GLAND RESECTION    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME    REMOVE_MRN     left adrenal gland   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 4cm soft tissue mass  surrounded by fibroadipose tissue which weighs 325 gm  There is focal capsular  disruption identified by the surgeon in the frozen section room  The area of  capsular disruption is inked blue while the rest of the specimen is inked black   The specimen is bivalved through the area of capsular disruption to reveal an  8 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan brown  soft  friable mass with large areas of necrosis    50  of mass  and a focal REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm solid yellow area within the larger  mass  Representative sections of the solid yellow area is frozen as FX 1 and of  the tan brown more necrotic area is submitted as FX 1A  Vascular margins are  identified by the surgeon  A gross photograph is taken  Sectioning reveals the  mass grossly appears to be encapsulated by a thin capsule membrane in which the  membrane in some areas represents the inked black resection margin  No residual  normal adrenal parenchyma is identified     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FX 1  representative solid yellow area    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   FX 1A  representative tan brown area    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Vascular margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of viable mass       Immunohistochemical and in situ hybridization tests performed at Massachusetts  General Hospital have been developed and their performance characteristics  determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of  Pathology at Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or  approved by the U S Food and Drug Administration  FDA   the FDA has determined  that such clearance or approval is not necessary       PART   LEFT ADRENAL GLAND RESECTION       report_end  , No.
