Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 38 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  TWO FOCI  TOGETHER ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  RADIAL SCARS HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion are not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA INVOLVING ELEVEN OF THIRTY LYMPH NODES  AND EXTENDING INTO AXILLARY FAT  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL QUADRANT    EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  SEE NOTE  Note  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached axillary tail measuring REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 1 5cm and a suture  designating the superior aspect of the specimen  There is an attached skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 14 9cm which contains a 2 0cm well healed  linear scar immediately lateral to an unremarkable nipple  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a stellate shaped area of tan white  rubbery parenchyma with a hemorrhagic central area measuring 0 5cm  and 2 5cm from the nearest  superior  margin  The area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm and radiates to within 1 5cm of the nearest margin  superior  and 1 4cm from the deep margin  Separate from the area of the biopsy cavity by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm area of tan white  fibrous tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  focally cystic  firm mass 2 5cm away from the nearest  anterior  margin  The remaining uninvolved areas of parenchyma contain scattered areas of rubbery  tan white nodularity  The axillary lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm  SECTION CODE A  Nearest  anterior  margin  biopsy cavity  B E  Biopsy cavity  F H  Mass away from biopsy cavity  I  Nearest  anterior  margin  mass away from biopsy cavity  J K  Uninvolved parenchyma  L V  Axillary lymph nodes  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lateral quadrant right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unremarkable skin ellipse  The deep portion of the specimen contains multiple cysts 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The cysts are smooth walled and filled with straw colored fluid  Further sectioning of the specimen reveals unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with focal areas of tan white rubbery nodularity  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes W through FF with sections of cystic areas in BB through DD  Gross Description by  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  CYSTS  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  LATERAL QUADRANT    EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Not_reported.
