Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  NUCCI  MARISA  ROSE  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by NUCCI MARISA ROSE M D   RIGHT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  three separate foci  measuring 0 8cm  0 5cm   and less than 0 1cm  well differentiated  modified Bloom Richardson  grade I III   See NOTE   No lymphatic vascular invasion identified   Margins are free of invasive carcinoma   LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   Healing biopsy site   Note  The largest focus of invasive carcinoma shows minor ductal  differentiation  The carcinoma in situ associated with this focus also  shows minor ductal differentiation  These areas of carcinoma in situ  showing ductal differentiation are not present at or near a margin   Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptors  progesterone  receptors  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu will be performed and reported in an addendum   AJCC  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID b Nx Mx with multiple foci of invasion   CLINICAL DATA   History  None given   Operation  Right breast biopsy  Clinical Diagnosis  Abnormal mammogram  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Right needle directed breast biopsy  RADIOLOGY  Mass is in the specimen      Dr  C  Denison  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by LEE BENJAMIN H  M D  PH D   The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit  number and  right breast biopsy needle   and consists of one fragment of  pink yellow fibroadipose tissue  5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm   with a needle localization  wire in place and two orienting sutures  the long denoting lateral and the  short denoting superior margin  The specimen is inked by the frozen section  resident  The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins  posterior    black  anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow   medial   orange  Sections of margins are sub