nd the radiologic calcifications  in an area measuring 4 to 5cm in size   The residual invasive carcinoma is similar in appearance to the pre treatment  carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    but is less cellular  The carcinoma appears viable and  mitotic figures are present  Immunohistochemical studies will be repeated and  reported in an addendum  The residual DCIS consists of scattered and focally  clustered markedly pleomorphic cells in ducts   This would be considered a Miller Payne Grade 4 response   CLINICAL DATA   History  38 year old female with  R  breast carcinoma  s p chemo  carboplatin   Taxotere  Herceptin   negative sentinal lymph node bx   Operation  Right simple mastectomy   Operative Findings  None given   Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast cancer   TISSUE SUBMITTED   A 1  Right simple mastectomy   stitch on lower axillary node   GROSS DESCRIPTION   The specimen is received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number   and  Right simple mastectomy   stitch on lower axillary node   and consists of  a REMOVED_DATE gm simple mastectomy specimen  16 0 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm   with a tan  wrinkled skin ellipse  14 6 x 7 2cm    The tan nipple  1 3cm in greatest  dimension  is everted with focal purple gray discoloration  The areola   3 5cm in greatest dimension  is tan brown  No scar is grossly identified on  the epithelial surface  Per surgeon  there is a stitch designating the  lower  axillary node   The deep margin  inked black  is a smooth fascial plane  The  specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  and is radiographed per  prosector in the surgical pathology cutting room  In the central superior  breast  approximately 12 o clock   there is an irregular poorly delineated firm  white fibrous area  0 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm   3 4cm superior deep to the nipple and  1 8cm from the deep margin  This area was previously sampled by the tissue  bank in the frozen section room  1 6cm inferior anterior to the  aforementioned firm