Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 10 CLINICAL DATA  Forty eight year old woman with DCIS left breast  for reexcision today                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  NOTE  Tumor is present throughout the specimen and abuts the inked superior and inferior margins in several foci  the tumor is predominantly cribiform type but foci comedo and apocrine type carcinoma are also present  Pagetoid intraductal spread is also identified  2  SCAR AND BIOPSY CAVITY  3  MICROCALCIFICATION  4  FOCAL ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA WITH PAGETOID INTRADUCTAL SPREAD  Diagnosis by  Fiona M  Graeme Cook  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 15 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  Only intraductal carcinoma is present in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the corresponding values were 97  and 95   respectively  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 breast carcinomas with determination of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy nine percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 97  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm skin ellipse with underlying breast tissue  excised to a maximum depth of 3 5cm  One stitch is present along the long axis of the skin and two are present at one pole  The epidermal surface displays a REMOVED_DATE x less than 0 1cm logitudinal scar at its center  The superior aspect of the specimen is inked green and the inferior aspect of the specimen is inked yellow  The specimen is sectioned revealing a 0 3cm in diameter  irregular  firm  tan white nodule at the deep inferior aspect  midway between the superior and inferior aspects  The inferior aspect of the specimen is white and rubbery  At the mid point of the specimen is a 0 4cm in diameter red tan area  0 9cm deep to the scar  This region is 1 6cm from the deep resection margin  Section Code A   superior end B   inferior end C   irregular firm tan nodule  inferior  D K   representative breast from superior to inferior Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  SMALL SUSPICIOUS AREA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL 